      "value": "I spent some more time digging on this, and found the actual bug. If a contact is turned off and back on within the same frame, all existing collisions are dropped and not properly recreated. Presumably this happens in-game during avatar scaling, and possibly other edge cases, which is why it occurs periodically.\n\nIt looks like OnReenableInCollisionScene was originally written to handle this \"cancelled removal\" situation, but it only sets the parameter value once, and doesn't actually rebuild the collision list, so the next tick there are no active collisions and the value becomes zero.\n\nHere's a reproduction. Add the component to a gameobject in play mode, and it should log 1,1,1, but instead it logs 1,0,1.\n\n```\n\nusing System.Collections;\n\nusing UnityEngine;\n\nusing VRC.Dynamics;\n\nusing VRC.SDK3.Dynamics.Contact.Components;\n\npublic class ContactOverlapBug : MonoBehaviour {\n\n    IEnumerator Start() {\n\n        var s = new GameObject(\"Sender\").AddComponent<VRCContactSender>();\n\n        var r = new GameObject(\"Receiver\").AddComponent<VRCContactReceiver>();\n\n        s.transform.SetParent(transform, false);\n\n        r.transform.SetParent(transform, false);\n\n        s.allowInit = r.allowInit = true;\n\n        s.radius = r.radius = 0.2f;\n\n        s.collisionTags.Add(\"Repro\");\n\n        r.collisionTags.Add(\"Repro\");\n\n        r.receiverType = ContactReceiver.ReceiverType.Proximity;\n\n        yield return new WaitForSeconds(0.2f);\n\n        Debug.Log(\"Before: \" + r.paramValue); // 1\n\n        r.enabled = false;\n\n        transform.localScale *= 2;\n\n        r.enabled = true;\n\n        yield return new WaitForSeconds(0.5f);\n\n        Debug.Log(\"After receiver turns off and back on: \" + r.paramValue);\n\n        s.transform.position = r.transform.position + Vector3.one * 10;\n\n        yield return new WaitForSeconds(0.2f);\n\n        s.transform.position = r.transform.position;\n\n        yield return new WaitForSeconds(0.2f);\n\n        Debug.Log(\"After receiver is moved and moved back: \" + r.paramValue);\n\n    }\n\n}\n\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
